From: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:17:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tests: retain KV revisions until the stream source copies them

The KV source test writes three revisions and expects all three to reach
an asynchronous source stream, but the default KV history retains only
the latest revision. A fast second update can evict value2 before the
source copies it. Retain all three revisions while preserving the original
update ordering and all fetched-message content assertions.

Signed-off-by: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
 server/jetstream_test.go | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/jetstream_test.go b/server/jetstream_test.go
--- a/server/jetstream_test.go
+++ b/server/jetstream_test.go
@@ -12243,8 +12243,8 @@
 	nc, js := jsClientConnect(t, s)
 	defer nc.Close()
 
-	// Create a kv store
-	kv, err := js.CreateKeyValue(&nats.KeyValueConfig{Bucket: "test"})
+	// Retain all revisions until the asynchronous source can copy them.
+	kv, err := js.CreateKeyValue(&nats.KeyValueConfig{Bucket: "test", History: 3})
 	require_NoError(t, err)
 
 	// Create a stream with a source from the kv store
